WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.102
-Before we get to that,

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.370
the president threatened
to go to war with Congress

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.238
and now he
and his Attorney General

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.506
are doing exactly that.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.241
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.709
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.678 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.814
-For the first two years
of his presidency,

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.549
Trump enjoyed complete immunity

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.217
and freedom to do
whatever he wanted

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.319
because Republicans in Congress
let him get away with it.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.956
But then, after Democrats
won back control of the House

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.258
in November and gained the power
to investigate him,

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.893
Trump threatened to go to war.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.128
-If they start investigating
you,

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:30.897
can you compartmentalize that

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.332
and still continue
to work with them

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.500
for the benefit of the rest
of the country --

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.369
-No.
-Or are all bets off?

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.938
-No. If they do that,
then it's just --

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.041
All it is is a war-like posture.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.644
-I can't exactly imagine Trump
in a war-like posture.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.213
He spends most of his time
in a duck-like posture.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.815
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.349
If he were at
the Battle of Winterfell,

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:51.584
he wouldn't have been
on the front lines

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.085
or fighting a dragon.
He would have been

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:55.154
sitting under a tree
in his golf cart.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.455
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:58.324
But now Trump and his team

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.693
are showing us their
war-like posture

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.495
after his Attorney General
William Barr

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.163
refused to show up
for a hearing today

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.199
in the House Judiciary Committee
to answer questions

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.535
about Special Counsel Robert
Mueller's report.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.603
Barr refused to show up
specifically

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.706
because the committee wanted to
let lawyers ask him questions.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.608
-William Barr
informing the house panel

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.777
he will not testify today
as scheduled.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.813
He had been scheduled to testify
to the House Judiciary Committee

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.815
about his handling
of the Mueller report.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.450
But Barr rejected
the committee's plan

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.486
to have one of its staff lawyers

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.621
question him alongside
lawmakers.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.191
-We cannot permit
the administration to dictate

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.092
to Congress how we operate.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:37.030
He is terrified of having
to face a skilled attorney.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.498
-And I'm sure he is.
Usually when you work for Trump,

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.467
the only attorney you have
to face is this guy,

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.770
and he is definitely not
skilled.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.240
He looks like he can't believe
he's the president's lawyer.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.408
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.543
Rudy always looks like
the last frame of a clip

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.412
from "America's Funniest
Home Videos."

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.748
if you tuned in late and saw
this, you'd immediately say,

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.351
"Oh, that guy just got
hit in the nuts by a seesaw."

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.685
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.153
So with Barr
refusing to show up,

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.490
Democrats decided to make a show
of his cowardice

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.090
by holding a hearing with
an empty chair

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.292
where Barr would have been
sitting.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.627
And then immediately after
the hearing,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.762
Democrats used the opportunity
to slam Barr

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.197
for refusing to show up.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.531
-I don't feel that I can trust

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:14.767
anything that
the Attorney General is saying

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:18.471
because I don't know who
the Attorney General works for.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.805
-Attorney General Bill Barr

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:22.541
is now one of the most dangerous
men in Washington, D.C.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:24.844
-The so-called Attorney General

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:29.148
is abrasive, evasive,
and unpersuasive.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:32.018
-Man, this confirms
everyone's worst fear.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.486
If you don't show up to a party,

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:36.155
the people who do are gonna
talk [bleep] about you...

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Laughter and applause ]
...in rhyme!

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.829
But Democrats didn't stop
at just calling out Barr.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.965
Congressman Steve Cohen
decided to mock him

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.967
by putting a glass chicken
in Barr's place

00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:50.870
and bringing out a bucket
of KFC.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.938
And then he brought out
the chicken statue again

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:55.074
during an interview
after the hearing

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.609
to really hit the point home.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.610
-Representative Steve Cohen
of Tennessee

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.547
started eating a bucket
of Kentucky Fried Chicken

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:03.716
this morning while lawmakers
and the press

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.885
waited to see if Barr
would show up.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.654
-Tennessee Democrat Steve Cohen
then placed a chicken statue

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:11.624
and a bucket of KFC
in front of the empty chair,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.759
poking fun at Barr's refusal
to appear.

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.962
-Chicken Barr
should have shown up today

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.430
and answered questions.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.900
-We are looking at images of you
at that committee hearing today

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.702
with what appears to be a bucket
of fried chicken.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:23.770
And -- Oh, there it is.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.005
You brought props, I see,
with you here.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.574
What is the message
you're trying to send?

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.777
-The message is that Bill Barr
is a chicken.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.112
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.783
Is that the message? I'm, uh...

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.751
I'm not sure we got it, pal.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.019
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.922
Also, dude, if you want KFC,
just order KFC.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.791
It's fine. You don't need to
tie it into the hearing.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.760
"And he's probably not here
because he knew

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.229
we'd be hitting him with
a McFlurry of questions!"

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.999
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:56.769
So Barr decided not to show up,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.004
and yet Republicans
on the committee

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.205
still wanted time to complain.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.873
Not about Barr,
but about the Democrats,

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.475
like Congressman Matt Gaetz.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.143
Gaetz tried to interrupt
the committee chairman

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.445
as he was wrapping up
the hearing,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.213
but he was only able to get
a few words in

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.647
before his mic was cut off.

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:10.983
-We need the information without
delay.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.952
The hearing is adjourned.
-Mr. chairman, I --

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.554
-And we'll do so with trampling
minority rights.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:18.891
-It's gonna be, Mr. Chairman,
where there's not going to be

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:22.495
a recognition of members
who seek legitimate inquiry

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.397
as to the procedures --

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.498
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.498 --> 00:04:28.534
-Wow, forget muting someone
on Twitter.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.937
Turns out you can mute him
in real life.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.471
Seriously,
can we please try that

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:34.006
next time Trump holds a rally?

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:37.309
-Look, it's a rigged system.
Okay?

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:40.079
If I told you how --

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.113
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:42.815
-So, that was it. That was it.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.352
Barr just refused to show up
and answer questions

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.520
about how he handled

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.155
one of the most
highly anticipated reports

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.456
in modern political history.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.258
And that might be because
when he faced

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.260
skilled questioning
from experienced Senators

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.328
in a hearing yesterday,
he often had no answer.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:57.697
Like when Senator Kamala Harris

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.431
asked Barr if anyone
in the White House

00:04:59.431 --> 00:05:02.401
had ever asked him to open
an investigation into anyone,

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:05.237
and Barr clearly did not
want to answer the question.

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.439
-Has the president or anyone
at the White House

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:11.744
ever asked or suggested that you
open an investigation of anyone?

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.612
Yes or no, please, sir.

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:18.117
-Um, the president
or anybody else?

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.553
-It seems you'd remember
something like that

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.154
and be able to tell us.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.957
-Yeah, but I'm trying to grapple
with the word "suggest."

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:28.194
I mean, there have been
discussions of matters

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:31.463
out there that --
They have not asked me

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:33.633
to open an investigation,
but --

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.434
-Perhaps they've suggested?
-I don't know.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:37.236
I wouldn't say suggest.
-Hinted?

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:41.540
-I don't know.
-Inferred?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.175
You don't know? Okay.

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:46.078
-If it takes you that long
to answer something,

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:47.212
the answer is yes.

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:49.781
If you go in
for your performance review

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:51.383
at Chipotle and your boss says,

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:52.951
"Just one last question, Brad.

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:55.788
Have you ever wrapped
your genitals in a tortilla?"

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.556
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:00.293
And Brad says, "Uh...

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.228
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:05.898
I'm trying to...

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.134
trying to grapple with the word
'wrap,'"

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.535
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:12.071
the answer is yes,

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.373
Brad wrapped his [bleep]
in a tortilla.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:17.276
That happened.

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:19.144
So Barr lied about
Mueller's findings

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:21.080
before anyone else
got to see them.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.149
That's why Mueller
sent his letter to Barr

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.583
complaining about the process.

00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:25.818
A letter he sent in March,

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.220
but which we only found out
about this week.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.857
And when he was asked about that
letter at his hearing yesterday,

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.458
Barr basically just
shrugged it off

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.593
and specifically complained
about the tone.

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:36.562
-This letter was
an extraordinary act.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:39.565
A career prosecutor rebuking

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.967
the Attorney General
of the United States.

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:43.803
I know of no other instance of
--

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:45.905
But he was also
a political appointee

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.573
and he was a political appointee
with me

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.975
at the Department of Justice.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:51.910
I don't -- you know,
the letter is a bit snitty,

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.179
and I think it was
probably written

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:54.813
by one of his staff people.

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:56.349
-Sorry, did you call it snitty?

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:59.819
Are you the Attorney General
or the Dowager Countess?

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:01.120
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.221
Also, you know, of course
he was snitty.

00:07:03.221 --> 00:07:05.691
He spent two years
working on a 400-page report

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.892
about a criminal conspiracy

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:08.461
to interfere
in a presidential election,

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:11.230
and then you wrote a four-page
summary lying about it.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.230
I'd be snitty, too.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.833
It's like if Michelangelo

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:15.267
unveiled the Sistine Chapel,

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:17.503
and then the pope just put
a plaque under it that said

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.838
"Two Dudes Touching Fingers."

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.439
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:22.375
So Barr lied to the American
people and to Congress,

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:24.743
and now he's just not showing up
to hearings at all,

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:26.278
which means the next thing
Congress should do

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:28.147
is call Mueller himself
to testify

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.816
so we can actually hear from
the guy who wrote the report.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.251
Democrats in the House --

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.652
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:35.921
Democrats in the house
have said they want to do that.

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:37.990
But in the Senate, Republican
Senator Lindsey Graham,

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.391
chairman of
the Judiciary Committee,

00:07:39.391 --> 00:07:42.227
said flat-out he definitely will
not call Mueller to testify.

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:44.163
-Why not call for Mueller
to testify?

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:47.132
-Because I'm not going to do
anymore.

00:07:47.132 --> 00:07:49.668
Enough already. It's over.

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:52.104
-No, it's not over just because
you said it's over.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:54.040
We should hear from Mueller,
because for one thing,

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.340
we never do.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:57.476
I mean, I don't even know
what his voice sounds like.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:59.945
Maybe he sounds
like Bobcat Goldthwait

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:02.381
from "Police Academy."

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.350
-[ Zany voice ] And I'd like
to discuss with you something

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.184
that would be vital
for you to know.

00:08:06.184 --> 00:08:07.586
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:07.586 --> 00:08:09.355
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:11.357 line:0%
♪♪

